//@version=4
study("UCTPROBE_VW_TC1_COLOUR_NA_COMPARE", overlay = false)

// --- 2026-11-16 text-colour unit (TC) - a COLOUR compared with `na`, and two colours compared ---
//
// engulfing-sinyal (v4) writes `alertcondition(Bueng != na, ...)` where `Bueng` is
// `<condition> ? color.yellow : na`. What TradingView answers for `<colour> != na`,
// `<colour> == na` and `na(<colour>)` is not captured, so the runtime lane refuses a colour
// compared with `na` by name (`runtime:colour`, "a colour compared with `na`"). Each row below is
// its own plot of 1 / 0, so the capture records the answer bar by bar:
//
//   C1  colour != na          C2  colour == na          C3  na(colour)
//   N1  number != na          N2  number == na          N3  na(number)     (the same three on a NUMBER,
//                                                                            so a reader can tell a colour
//                                                                            rule from the general `na` rule)
//   E1  color.new(red, 50.1) == color.new(red, 50.2)    one opacity byte (128), two transparencies: does
//                                                        TradingView compare the byte (1) or the number (0)?
//                                                        The runtime lane refuses this shape by name until then.
//   E2  color.rgb(255, 82, 82) == color.red             the same colour spelled two ways (v4 red is #FF5252):
//                                                        a control that must read 1 on every bar
//   B0  bar_index             (control: the capture's bars are the bars we compute on)
//
// CAPTURE: NYSE:RDDT 1D from the listing, inputs at defaults, after the close, with
// tools/vendor_harness/tv_capture.js. If a row does not compile on v4 (C3 is the likeliest),
// record the compile error text and remove only that row, as the B1 probe did for D1.

up = close > open
c = up ? color.yellow : na
x = up ? close : na

plot(c != na ? 1 : 0, "C1")
plot(c == na ? 1 : 0, "C2")
plot(x != na ? 1 : 0, "N1")
plot(x == na ? 1 : 0, "N2")
plot(na(x) ? 1 : 0, "N3")
plot(color.new(color.red, 50.1) == color.new(color.red, 50.2) ? 1 : 0, "E1")
plot(color.rgb(255, 82, 82) == color.red ? 1 : 0, "E2")
plot(bar_index, "B0")
plot(na(c) ? 1 : 0, "C3")
